# mv Command (Move / Rename)

`mv` is used to **move** files/directories or **rename** them.

---

## Rename a File

```bash
mv old.txt new.txt


# Examples

Move a File to Another Directory
mv file.txt /home/user/Documents/

Rename a Directory
mv oldfolder newfolder



| Command | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| `mv old.txt new.txt` | rename a file |
| `mv file.txt /path/` | move file to another directory |
| `mv file1.txt file2.txt /path/` | move multiple files |
| `mv -i file.txt /path/` | ask before overwriting |
| `mv -v file.txt /path/` | show what is being moved |

